gpu_frame_stats on Vulkan: host GPU time per frame by category. A timestamp is written at every render pass entry
and exit and wherever the command processor starts or stops IssueDraw's render target update, IssueCopy (resolves)
or IssueSwap, always outside a render pass so its query can be reset just before; the time between two consecutive
timestamps of a submission goes to the category the first one opened: draw passes, render target updates
(ownership transfers, clears), resolves, swap (gamma, FXAA, presentation copy) or other (barriers, uploads, texture
loads between passes). The DeferredCommandBuffer learns vkCmdWriteTimestamp.

